{"title":"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc701ad9b432b3bdb5b3c1b0d2d47aa001998149.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  pair A=dir(0),B=dir(80),C=dir(160),D=dir(310),O=(0,0); draw(circle(O,1),black); draw(A--B--C--D--A--C--B--D);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Suppose n points on the circumference of a circle\nare joined by straight line segments in all possible ways\nand that no point that is not one of the original n points\nis contained in more than two of the segments. How\nmany triangles are formed by the segments? Count all\ntriangles whose sides lie along the segments, including\ntriangles that overlap with other triangles. For example,\nfor n = 3, there is one triangle and for n = 4 (shown\nin the diagram), there are 8 triangles.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairwise intersecting <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">lines</a> make a triangle, so we can split the possibilities into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases:\n</p><p><b>Case 1: All vertices of the triangle are points on the circle</b>\n</p><p>Any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points will work, so it's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d65d0667888aee4f6bd611ab578a9cd45ac51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${n}\\choose{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60b555218020ee3adfdf241fcc3a11dded958a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  pair A=dir(0),B=dir(80),C=dir(160); draw(unitcircle); draw(A--B--C--A);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case 2: 2 vertices of the triangle are points on the circle</b>\n</p><p>There will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points to choose from, but you also have to multiply by the number of orientations (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/9/c59e882344f5a80c99a391b3e45e9fa77e23a4c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${n}\\choose{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/1275686b379efab9cd03a6931abf00c04cd8db82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  pair A=dir(0),B=dir(80),C=dir(160),D=dir(310); draw(unitcircle); draw(A--C--B--D);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><b>Case 3: 1 vertex of the triangle is a point on the circle</b>\n</p><p>There will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points to choose from, but you also have to multiply by the number of orientations (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/392d67e4665113ed916f46c304258d529ae03437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${n}\\choose{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97fbc903b64f0133f3b81d436356656fec250003.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  pair A=dir(0),B=dir(80),C=dir(160),D=dir(210),E=dir(300); draw(unitcircle); draw(A--C--E); draw(B--D);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><b>Case 4: All vertices of the triangle are not points on the circle</b>\n</p><p>Any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points will work, so it's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48badc191db43de4c294ec19b2f770fa4ff4ea25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${n}\\choose{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6ff400ddd21a5718a4e1953b1db4a6888454e6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  pair A=dir(0),B=dir(130),C=dir(160),D=dir(210),E=dir(270),F=dir(320); draw(unitcircle); draw(A--D); draw(B--E); draw(C--F);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Thus there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01455f3be109f0770cc4aa57b593cd17a6f5851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\binom{n}{6}+5\\binom{n}{5}+4\\binom{n}{4}+\\binom{n}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -29px\" width=\"254\" height=\"67\" /> different triangles.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II\">2017 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_Northern_Colorado_Math_Contest\" title=\"University of Northern Colorado Math Contest\"> All UNCO Math Contest Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018004029\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 157/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1409/2097152 bytes\nTemplate 